Connecting the MDC Cable

1. Connect the RS232 cable (or RJ45-to-Serial cable depending on model) between the PC/controller and the Samsung ePaper display.
2. If using TCP/IP MDC:
    * Connect both the display and controller system to the same network.
    * Enable MDC over Network from the display settings.
3. Configure communication settings:
    * Baud Rate: 9600
    * Data Bits: 8
    * Parity: None
    * Stop Bit: 1

⸻

Generic MDC Command Syntax

MDC commands follow this packet structure:

[Header][Command][Display ID][Data Length][Data][Checksum]

Field Description

Field	Description
Header	Fixed value 0xAA
Command	MDC command code
Display ID	Target display ID
Data Length	Length of data bytes
Data	Command parameters
Checksum	Sum of all bytes except Header (0xFF masked)

⸻

Generic Command Format

AA <Command> <ID> <Length> <Data> <Checksum>

Example — Power ON

AA 11 01 01 01 14

Byte	Meaning
AA	Header
11	Power command
01	Display ID
01	Data length
01	Power ON
14	Checksum

⸻

Checksum Formula

Checksum = (Command + ID + Length + Data bytes) & 0xFF

Example:

11 + 01 + 01 + 01 = 14

Hence checksum = 0x14.
